# Frontend Rules

## Stack
- React 19 + TypeScript (strict mode)
- Vite as bundler
- TailwindCSS for styling
- Zustand for global state
- React Query (TanStack) for async/Tauri command data fetching
- React Router for navigation

---

## Folder Structure

```
src/
├── main.tsx                        # App entry
├── App.tsx                         # Root router + providers
├── assets/                         # Static assets (icons, images)
├── styles/                         # Global CSS, Tailwind base
├── lib/
│   ├── tauri.ts                    # All invoke() calls live here — never call invoke() in a component
│   ├── utils.ts                    # Pure utility functions (formatBytes, truncatePath, etc.)
│   └── constants.ts                # App-wide constants
├── store/
│   └── bucketStore.ts              # Zustand stores (one file per domain)
├── hooks/
│   └── useBucketContents.ts        # Custom hooks wrapping React Query + tauri lib
├── types/
│   └── index.ts                    # All shared TypeScript types/interfaces
├── components/
│   └── ui/                         # Reusable primitives (Button, Modal, Spinner, etc.)
├── dashboard/
│   ├── Dashboard.tsx               # Route root for dashboard
│   ├── components/
│   │   ├── FileTable.tsx
│   │   ├── BreadcrumbBar.tsx
│   │   └── UploadDropzone.tsx
│   └── utils/
│       └── fileHelpers.ts          # Dashboard-specific utils only
├── settings/
│   ├── Settings.tsx                # Route root for settings
│   ├── components/
│   │   ├── BucketForm.tsx
│   │   └── ConnectionStatus.tsx
│   └── utils/
│       └── validateCredentials.ts
└── buckets/
    ├── BucketList.tsx
    ├── components/
    │   └── BucketCard.tsx
    └── utils/
```

Every feature/route gets its own folder at the top level.
Components shared across features go in `src/components/ui/`.
Never put business logic in a component — extract to a hook or util.

---

## Component Rules

- Functional components only, no class components
- One component per file, filename matches the component name exactly
- Props interface defined directly above the component, named `[ComponentName]Props`
- Default export for the main component, named exports for helpers in same file
- No inline anonymous functions passed as event handlers — extract and name them

```tsx
// GOOD
interface FileRowProps {
  file: BucketFile;
  onDelete: (key: string) => void;
}

export default function FileRow({ file, onDelete }: FileRowProps) {
  const handleDelete = () => onDelete(file.key);
  return <button onClick={handleDelete}>Delete</button>;
}

// BAD — no inline handlers, no unnamed props
export default function FileRow({ file, onDelete }: { file: any; onDelete: any }) {
  return <button onClick={() => onDelete(file.key)}>Delete</button>;
}
```

