## TypeScript

- `strict: true` in tsconfig — no exceptions
- No `any` — use `unknown` and narrow it
- All Tauri command return types must have a corresponding TS type in `src/types/index.ts`
- Prefer `interface` for object shapes, `type` for unions/aliases

```ts
// src/types/index.ts
export interface BucketFile {
  key: string;
  size: number;
  lastModified: string;
  etag: string;
}

export interface BucketConnection {
  id: string;
  label: string;
  provider: "r2" | "minio" | "s3" | "b2" | "wasabi";
  endpoint: string;
  bucket: string;
  accessKeyId: string;
  secretAccessKey: string;
}
```

---

## Styling

- Tailwind utility classes only — no inline `style={}` unless dealing with dynamic values that Tailwind can't handle (e.g. dynamic widths from JS)
- Component variants use `clsx` or `cva` — not ternary class strings
- No CSS modules, no styled-components
- Design tokens live in `tailwind.config.ts` — never hardcode hex values in JSX

```tsx
// GOOD
import { clsx } from "clsx";

const buttonClass = clsx(
  "px-4 py-2 rounded-md text-sm font-medium",
  variant === "danger" && "bg-red-500 text-white hover:bg-red-600",
  variant === "ghost" && "bg-transparent text-zinc-400 hover:text-white"
);

// BAD
<button style={{ color: "#ef4444" }} className={"px-4 " + (danger ? "bg-red-500" : "bg-zinc-800")}>
```

---

## Error Handling

- All async operations wrapped in try/catch with typed errors
- Use a shared `handleTauriError(e: unknown): string` util in `src/lib/utils.ts`
- Surface errors via toast notifications (one toast lib, configured in `App.tsx`)
- Never `console.error` raw objects in production paths — log the message

---

## Do Not

- Do not call `invoke()` outside `src/lib/tauri.ts`
- Do not create a new util function if one already exists — search `src/lib/utils.ts` first
- Do not duplicate types — if it exists in `src/types/index.ts`, import it
- Do not nest components inside other component files
- Do not use `useEffect` for data fetching — use React Query
- Do not let any file exceed 300 lines — extract to a smaller component or hook
